  "as_of": "2023-09-07",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would let eligible royal commissions use suitably qualified senior staff as Assistant Commissioners to conduct private sessions with people sharing personal experiences.",
   "A sole commissioner or commission chair would need to authorise the appointment in writing and consider that circumstances justify allowing the staff member to hold sessions.",
   "The changes would apply to existing and future royal commissions from the day after Royal Assent, while private session confidentiality arrangements would continue."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Assistant Commissioners conducting sessions would receive protection and immunity equivalent to a High Court justice.",
   "Assistant Commissioners could authorise other people to attend a private session.",
   "Contempt provisions would extend to sessions conducted by Assistant Commissioners."
  ],
  "affected": "Royal commissioners, eligible commission staff and people taking part in private sessions are affected.",
